### ============================================================
### SMS — End-to-end flow you can click through, top to bottom
### Open this file in VS Code with REST Client extension installed.
### Each "Send Request" link is grey text above a request.
### ============================================================

### Step 1 — Register a new STUDENT (public, no token needed)
POST http://localhost:5003/api/students
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Lavanya Badyal",
  "email": "lavanya.badyal@data.com",
  "password": "Lavanya123"
}


### Step 2 — Log in as that student to get a JWT
# @name studentLogin
POST http://localhost:5001/api/login/student
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "lavanya.badyal@data.com",
  "password": "Lavanya123"
}


### Step 3 — Copy the access_token from Step 2's response, paste below.
### Then send this to get your own profile.
GET http://localhost:5003/api/students/PASTE_YOUR_STUDENT_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN_HERE


### Step 4 — Try listing ALL students. This will FAIL with 403
### because students cannot list other students. That is the RBAC working.
GET http://localhost:5003/api/students
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### Admin flow — to create professors and courses, you need an admin token.
### One way: connect to your MongoDB Atlas, open the "students" collection,
### find your student record, and edit the role field to "admin".
### Then log in again. The new token will have role=admin.
### (Or, for the demo, you can directly insert an admin student.)
### ============================================================


### Step 5 — Create a PROFESSOR (admin only)
POST http://localhost:5002/api/professors
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "name": "Dr. Gunjan",
  "email": "gunjan@data.com",
  "phone": "555-0101",
  "password": "gunjan123"
}


### Step 6 — Log in as that professor
# @name professorLogin
POST http://localhost:5001/api/login/professor
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "gunjan@data.com",
  "password": "gunjan123"
}


### Step 7 — Create a COURSE owned by that professor
### (Use the professor token from Step 6)
POST http://localhost:5004/api/courses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_PROFESSOR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "code": "CS101",
  "name": "Intro to Computer Science",
  "description": "Basics of programming",
  "capacity": 30
}


### Step 8 — List all courses (any logged-in user can)
GET http://localhost:5004/api/courses
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ANY_TOKEN_HERE


### Step 9 — Enroll a student in a course (admin or professor)
POST http://localhost:5005/api/enrollments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_PROFESSOR_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "student": "PASTE_STUDENT_ID_HERE",
  "course": "PASTE_COURSE_ID_HERE"
}


### Step 10 — As the student, look at your own enrollments
GET http://localhost:5005/api/enrollments/student/PASTE_STUDENT_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN_HERE


### Step 11 — As the professor, see who is enrolled in your course
GET http://localhost:5005/api/enrollments/course/PASTE_COURSE_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_PROFESSOR_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### Update and delete examples
### ============================================================

### Update a student's own name/email
PUT http://localhost:5003/api/students/PASTE_STUDENT_ID_HERE
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_STUDENT_TOKEN_HERE

{
  "name": "Lavanya Updated"
}


### Delete a student (admin only)
DELETE http://localhost:5003/api/students/PASTE_STUDENT_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE


### ============================================================
### Quick health check
### ============================================================

### Confirm auth service is running and serving its public key
GET http://localhost:5001/.well-known/jwks.json
